    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4e0e9e58d23fa70d3915e8e2bafc027d37a22ac20f8c171d7deff56483878dac",
      "text": "After breakfast, travel by bus to Colca Canyon.\n\nThe canyon is about 3,500 m deep. Two active volcanoes stand nearby, and the canyon's origins are linked to their activity.\n\nThere will be several stops at viewpoints along the way.\n\nAt Lake Lagunillas, you can see pink flamingos.\n\nA stop for tea at the Canchis restaurant allows time to acclimatise.\n\nOne viewpoint offers a panorama of three volcanoes.\n\nArrive in Chivay and check in at the Colca Llacta 3* hotel.\n\nYou may visit the hot springs if you wish. There will also be time for lunch.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw2zik0k-amanda",
        "model": "GPT-6",
        "wordAbsenceReason": "The checked Word Colca paragraph omits the RU 3500-metre depth, two active volcanoes and Colca Llacta 3* accommodation; translate the assigned fuller RU text without changing its facts.",
        "wordSourceChecked": {
          "fileId": "1TxH9LDDzR5Bfjb0u_5CBmF_2N5kGi2ad",
          "documentSha256": "f5bcdb16d7149a4bd3f317cf9a84459111ff3c55704127c6f94c74b7323f2964"
        }
      }
    },
